<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 100.25 from 100.00, the Bundesbank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The move, effective immediately, brings the yield on the Series 123, 4.50 percent paper to 4.44 percent from 4.50 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
